<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cnut the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 990–1035</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Canute the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cnut the Great was a Danish prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweyn-forkbeard">Sweyn Forkbeard</a>, who conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1016 and became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1018 and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in 1028. Ruling this North Sea empire largely from England, he kept English law and institutions, used Danish and English earls and patronised the Church. His empire broke up soon after his death in 1035.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great.jpg" alt="Cnut the Great" width="296" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See Description (unknown) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canute_and_%C3%86lfgifu_cropped_(Canute).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
